WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.070
One of the things we've been talking about
in a sort of hypothetical sense since the

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:11.880
riots in Washington, DC on January 6th is
if instead of being a mostly white male conservative

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:17.100
crowd there, storming the Capitol, fighting
with police, pushing police with barriers,

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:22.210
hitting police with fire extinguishers and
on and on and on, if it had been a Black Lives

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:26.520
Matter protest, if the political orientation
had been different or the racial makeup of

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:30.700
the people there had been different, would
it have been allowed to go on for as long

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:31.700
as it did?

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:33.160
Would it have been handled in the same way?

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:38.340
And I think intuitively, most of us who understand
the way things have gone down in the United

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:42.550
States for the last many years can only come
to the conclusion that, no, it would not have

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:47.650
been the same if the protests last week had
been different groups of people in terms of

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:52.129
their makeup or politically oriented in a
different way.

00:00:52.129 --> 00:00:58.789
We don't just have to intuit our sense of
that because we actually have a study about

00:00:58.789 --> 00:00:59.789
this.

00:00:59.789 --> 00:01:02.260
And Barack Obama shared this on his Twitter
account recently.

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:09.319
And the study was lead was done by Acleda
ACL said it's a data reporting project and

00:01:09.319 --> 00:01:10.860
it looked initially.

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:15.380
They used to look at armed conflicts in African
countries and then they started looking at

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:16.380
the United States.

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:22.029
And in the United States, we've had so many
protests, riots of different kinds, that there's

00:01:22.029 --> 00:01:26.069
plenty of fodder and data to look at.

00:01:26.069 --> 00:01:35.249
And what Occlude found is that law enforcement
is much more likely to try to shut down left

00:01:35.249 --> 00:01:41.349
wing protests than they are right wing protests
when law and.

00:01:41.349 --> 00:01:45.200
It uses force to shut them down.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:51.819
They are much more likely to use force in
the left wing protests than in the right wing

00:01:51.819 --> 00:01:57.740
protest by a 51 percent to 34 percent margin,
more than half the time when they decide to

00:01:57.740 --> 00:01:59.109
shut down a left wing protest.

00:01:59.109 --> 00:02:03.630
They use force only about a third of the time
when they decide to shut down a right wing

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:05.809
protest, they use force.

00:02:05.809 --> 00:02:10.379
And there are a number of different things
to consider here.

00:02:10.379 --> 00:02:17.599
You might say, well, maybe the left wing protests
are more violent and thus it makes sense that

00:02:17.599 --> 00:02:21.280
police are more likely to try to shut them
down or to use force.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:23.689
That is not what the data actually shows.

00:02:23.689 --> 00:02:30.860
The data does not show that left wing protests
are more violent than right wing protests.

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:36.709
Another consideration would be where are the
left wing versus the right wing protests taking

00:02:36.709 --> 00:02:37.709
place?

00:02:37.709 --> 00:02:39.200
In other words, political orientation.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:46.150
Of the protest aside, are the left wing protests
happening in places whose police departments,

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:50.659
for other reasons, are more likely to prevent
them from going on too long?

00:02:50.659 --> 00:02:51.750
Where is the right wing?

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:55.260
Protests are happening in places whose police
departments are more lax in allowing them

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:56.260
to go on.

00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:59.749
That also does not appear to be the case.

00:02:59.749 --> 00:03:03.260
And so this is a really a concern.

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:06.680
This is not a trivial thing.

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:15.120
And and where I believe much of the investigation
needs to be is in the political orientation,

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:20.439
not just of the police officers, but of the
police departments.

00:03:20.439 --> 00:03:22.620
And this also includes mayors.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:27.360
We know that law enforcement is a relatively
conservative group.

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:33.189
Law enforcement in total supported Trump in
twenty twenty at a much greater level than

00:03:33.189 --> 00:03:34.469
the average population.

00:03:34.469 --> 00:03:39.829
So, of course, there are liberal police departments
and police departments with liberal police

00:03:39.829 --> 00:03:41.849
chiefs or that work under liberal mayors.

00:03:41.849 --> 00:03:43.989
There's no doubt about that.

00:03:43.989 --> 00:03:48.629
But overall, the makeup of the officers tends
to be far more right wing than the average

00:03:48.629 --> 00:03:49.629
population.

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:53.920
This also applies to the military, although
we did see in twenty twenty that the military

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:59.249
was more supportive of Joe Biden than they've
been of of most past Democratic candidates,

00:03:59.249 --> 00:04:01.730
at least going back a number of elections.

00:04:01.730 --> 00:04:08.770
So certainly we have to consider whether the
political orientation of the officers plays

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:10.159
a role.

00:04:10.159 --> 00:04:17.139
And also if you have right wing officers,
but a more centrist or center left police

00:04:17.139 --> 00:04:21.720
chief and mayor, how does that affect the
handling of protesters?

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:29.220
What we know is that when we talk about the
right to protest, if the left wing protests

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:35.220
aren't more violent and we know that they
are not, but yet police are more like, oh,

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:41.340
and the left wing protesters are not more
likely to be armed and they are not, then

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:45.820
we have to say, well, why is it that the left
wing protests are more likely to be shot down?

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:46.820
And is that it?

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:48.380
Is that a restriction of speech?

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:54.470
And we've seen right wingers either misunderstand
or pretend not to understand when the First

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:55.470
Amendment is a factor.

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:58.570
You know, Twitter suspending Trump is not
a First Amendment issue.

00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:00.810
It has nothing to do with the First Amendment.

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:04.560
We hear all the time my First Amendment rights,
my First Amendment rights trumps First Amendment

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:07.400
rights when it has nothing to do with the
First Amendment.

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:14.419
When you see a political discrepancy in which
protests are shut down along the lines of

00:05:14.419 --> 00:05:18.830
the political orientation or motivations of
the protest by police, under the guidance

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:24.900
of police chiefs, city councils, mayors, ET,
you really actually have to start asking questions

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:28.490
about whether the government is suppressing
speech and suppressing it along political

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:29.490
lines.

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:31.680
So none of this is is a catch.

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:36.650
All that explains every circumstance, but
it's a very good data analysis.

00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:39.180
538 has a write up about it.

00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:45.849
Again, the organization that did the analysis
is Acleda a lead and will link to the article

00:05:45.849 --> 00:05:50.600
about it in the description on the YouTube
clip for this story.

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:51.600
Take a look at it.

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:52.600
Let me know what you think.

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:53.900
You can find me on Twitter at David Pakman,
The David Pakman Show at David Pakman Dotcom.

